  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Viet Nam: Improving Responsible Labour Practices and Supply Chain Transparency in the Natural Stone Industry (Phase 1)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will examine the obstacles and enabling factors for the natural stone processing and exporting businesses in Viet Nam, to address human and labour rights risks through implementing responsible recruitment and employment practices post COVID-19. Results of the project will help stakeholders involved in the natural stone industry in Viet Nam. In order to drive sustainable industry change, findings from the project will be made public and can be used to influence short and long-term policies and narrative related to responsible practices of workers employed in the natural stone supply chains, adopted by both private and public sector. This in turns will assist the business community in the natural stone industry in Viet Nam to gain more opportunities to join global supply chains by demonstrating greater transparency, fair recruitment and employment practices.</narrative>
  </description>
